				138,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Advance Element removing Cocoon file event stubs and normalizing Mountain IPC handlers\n\nAdvance the Element submodule (392f0aef → 346e1280) with a coordinated fix and refactor across Cocoon and Mountain.\n\n**Cocoon file event stub removal (fix):**\nSix stub handlers on the Workspace namespace (onWillCreateFiles, onWillDeleteFiles, onWillRenameFiles, onDidCreateFiles, onDidDeleteFiles, onDidRenameFiles) were returning no-op disposables, overriding the real EventSubscriber implementations from BuildDocumentEventMembers. Extensions subscribing to these events — including GitLens — received dead handlers that emitted nothing. Remove the stubs so live file lifecycle events flow through, with Mountain now firing willCreate/willDelete/willRename notifications via Vine before VFS mutation.\n\n**Mountain IPC handler normalization (refactor):**\nRename the three Cocoon IPC entry points from descriptive names (CocoonExtensionHostMessage, CocoonNotify, CocoonRequest) to the uniform Fn ident, with matching as aliases in mod.rs re-exports preserving downstream caller compatibility. Add four new ExtensionHost IPC handlers also exporting as Fn: DebugServiceClose (sky://exthost/debug-close via Tauri Emitter), DebugServiceReload (SkyEvent::ExtHostDebugReload), StarterCreate (stub extension-host ID), and StarterStart (real Cocoon PID for debugger attachment).\n\nAll handler modules now follow a single naming convention, eliminating guesswork when adding new IPC routes.",
			"SHA": "f82058e021c2365d8fb91329f9c42d1aef397e26"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T10:31:30Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				138,
				1
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Advance Element with Cocoon bootstrap reorder and Mountain extension cache\n\nAdvance the Element submodule (a27b4a9f → 392f0aef) carrying a coordinated fix and performance improvement across Cocoon and Mountain.\n\n**Cocoon bootstrap stage reordering (fix):**\nStage 3 MountainConnection (gRPC probe) previously ran ahead of Stage 5 RPCServer in the bootstrap pipeline, causing Mountain's 20-second gRPC retry budget to exhaust on every startup since port 50052 was never bound within the connect window. Swap execution order in `makeBootstrap` so RPCServer binds first, then MountainConnection connects to a live listener. Reduce retry caps proportionally: TCP probe from 10 to 3 attempts, gRPC connect from 15 to 5 attempts.\n\n**Mountain extension metadata cache (perf):**\nBuilding the serialised `ILocalExtension[]` array on every `extensions:getInstalled` IPC call re-serialised ~1.8 MB of extension metadata, causing multi-hundred-millisecond UI stalls on startup. Add a `OnceLock`-backed static cache keyed by TypeFilter variant. First call per type populates the cache; subsequent calls return a cloned `Value` in <1 ms. Empty responses are not cached to avoid poisoning on first-call timeout.\n\n**Mountain reliability fixes:**\n- `FileCloneNative` creates the target parent directory via `tokio::fs::create_dir_all` before `fs::copy`, resolving ENOENT failures for VS Code per-file history directories.\n- CocoonManagement IO forwarders switch from `tokio::spawn` to `tauri::async_runtime::spawn` so forwarder tasks persist while the spawning async task awaits elsewhere.\n\n**Build (Mountain):**\nAdd `Proto/Vine.proto` to `tauri.conf.json` resource globs so the .proto file is available at runtime from `Contents/Resources/`.\n\nAll changes are bounded by existing gRPC retry and timeout contracts — no runtime behaviour regressions.",
			"SHA": "37dafa2d5df993a36d4a3ef441f0ef8247d204a0"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-22T08:40:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				138,
				2
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Land): Migrate biome.json configuration to includes with negation\n\nReplace the deprecated `files.ignore` array with `files.includes` using the newer Biome configuration API. An explicit `includes: [\"**\"]` base pattern followed by negated globs (`!Element/*/Configuration/**`, `!Documentation/**`, etc.) reproduces the original exclusion set identically.\n\nAdvance the Element submodule (a27b4a9f) bringing:\n- Extension webview panel fix (Mountain/Sky): blank secondary panels now served via localhost URL with a dedicated WebviewHost.astro shell and window.opener.postMessage IPC bridge.\n- Bootstrap Cocoon bundle (Cocoon): self-contained npm-inlined bundle for .app deployment without a node_modules dependency tree.\n- Code quality: Cocoon subprocess env/I/O extraction into named functions, Air unused-import removal, stub IPC handlers for browserView and extensionHostStarter to prevent caller hangs.\n- Style normalisation (Output/Wind/Worker): tabs to 2-space conversion, import ordering, multi-line export collapse — zero behaviour change.\n\nNo runtime regressions.",
			"SHA": "5312a7d002e1a313cff11ebc7402caf570a721c5"
		}
	],
